docker run --rm -v "D:/Akshat/LadderLens_v6/LadderLens_v6/main":/work -w /work ladderlens:latest /bin/sh scripts/demo.sh

== Environment
algorithm      SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s-MTL-SHA2-128
MTL reference  commit 7cef0191da55, built with -O2 -g -fPIC

== 1. A synthetic signed zone
1450 RRsets (A 624, TXT 286, AAAA 337, MX 203); signing input 73 to 203 bytes per RRset

== 2. Arm C: sign 100 RRsets as one MTL batch (one SLH-DSA signature in total)
batch signed in 0.65 s; ladder 7,992 B; condensed signatures 108 to 172 B

== 3. Arm A: the same zone with plain SLH-DSA (5 of the 100 RRsets timed)
0.65 s per signature, so about 65 s for all 100 (extrapolated); each signature 7,856 B

== 4. What one DNS answer weighs
plain SLH-DSA                    7,970 B  exceeds 1,232 B
MTL full (no ladder cached)      8,279 B  exceeds 1,232 B
MTL condensed (ladder cached)      287 B  fits 1,232 B
verify: plain 0.63 ms, MTL cold 0.61 ms, MTL warm 3.7 µs per record

== 5. One resolver, 2,000 queries, the zone grows twice
1,997 hits, 3 ladder fetches, 177 B of signature per query (plain: 7,856 B); 17 answers verified on an older ladder after growth

== Next
make plan && make bench RUN=results/final && make report RUN=results/final
